hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2672","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Hisham, who narrated to us Hushaym, from Mansur, and Abd al-Malik, and Ibn Abi Layla, and al-Hajjaj, all of them from Ata, from Ya'la ibn Umayya (RA), who reported: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wearing a cloak that had traces of saffron on it. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I have entered the state of ihram"","" what is your view? The people are mocking me.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) paused for a moment"","" then called him and said: \""Take off this cloak from you"","" wash this saffron off your person"","" and perform your umrah in the same manner you performed your hajj.\""\nIt is additionally reported that al-Hajjaj stated at the end of this narration: Ata related this hadith to us from Safwan ibn Ya'la"","" from his father. And Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us"","" Hushaym narrated to us from al-Hajjaj"","" from Ata"","" who said: \""Before this hadith reached us"","" we would say [the man] should tear his cloak. But when this hadith reached us"","" we acted in accordance with it.\"""""""
